dependencies {
    // 47.4.22 and not 47.2.0: several mods used to test the integration (FTB Library, Easy NPC,
    // Carry On Extend) require 47.3+ or 47.4+, and with 47.2.0 the development client doesn't even start. It is the
    // same 1.20.1; mods.toml asks for no Forge version, so this doesn't change what the published
    // mod requires, only what it is compiled and tested with.
    minecraft 'net.minecraftforge:forge:1.20.1-47.4.22'
    // https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/io.github.tfriedrichs/dicebot
    minecraftLibrary 'io.github.tfriedrichs:dicebot:1.0.0'
    shade 'io.github.tfriedrichs:dicebot:1.0.0'

    // The "api" classifier and not the full jar: it is all that is needed to compile against Curios,
    // and it makes clear that its implementation is not depended on. An EARLY 5.x version is pinned on
    // purpose: the two methods that are used (CuriosApi.getCuriosInventory and getEquippedCurios) have existed
    // from the start, and compiling against the oldest is what makes the mod work with
    // whatever Curios the user has installed, not just the latest.
    compileOnly fg.deobf("top.theillusivec4.curios:curios-forge:5.4.7+1.20.1:api")

    // Pehkui 3.7.6, the OLDEST 1.20.1 published. The same criterion as Curios and Jade: the only thing that is
    // called (ScaleTypes.BASE.getScaleData().setScale/setTargetScale) has existed for many versions, and
    // compiling against the oldest is what makes any Pehkui the player has installed work.
    // t5W7Jfwy = the project; rUlbXz1h = that version.
    compileOnly fg.deobf("maven.modrinth:t5W7Jfwy:rUlbXz1h")

    // Jade 11.8.0, the OLDEST 1.20.1 that already has the current shape of the plugin API. The same criterion
    // as Curios and for the same reason: compiling against the oldest is what makes the mod
    // work with whatever Jade the player has installed, not just the latest. fg.deobf is needed because
    // the signatures of Jade's API name vanilla types (Entity, CompoundTag) and the published jar
    // ships them with SRG names.
    compileOnly fg.deobf("curse.maven:jade-324717:5072729")

    // Only the "api" artifact, which is all that is touched: PatchouliAPI.get().
    compileOnly fg.deobf("vazkii.patchouli:Patchouli:1.20.1-85-FORGE:api")

    // The full jar is NOT added as runtimeOnly. Tested, and the result is the same dead end as
    // with Curios, just one step further: put by hand in runClient/mods, Patchouli dies on
    // startup calling Minecraft.m_91087_() (the SRG name of getInstance) from its
    // BookCrashHandler; passed through fg.deobf, that call is fixed but its mixins fail, and
    // enabling mixin.env.remapRefMap to fix them breaks the mixins of any other production mod with
    // mixins loaded in the same client —Citadel the first one when it was tried—.
    // A development client cannot have deobfuscated mods and production mods with
    // mixins at the same time, and that is why runClient/mods stays empty (see above).
    //
    // So the Patchouli Guide is tested in a normal install with the built jar. What
    // is checked here is its structure: checkPatchouliBook requires every page of the Guide to be
    // in exactly one entry of the book, in both directions.

    // The full jar is NOT added as runtimeOnly, even though it would be handy for testing the integration:
